  "rationale": "Deploying mfa:admin alone is enough, and zero controls is not. Exfiltration needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Each of those needs a foothold via auth_db, auth_fileserver or auth_backup, all of which require stolen_dbadmin. The only sources of stolen_dbadmin are dump_dbadmin_dc and dump_dbadmin_adfs. These need admin_dc or admin_adfs, which need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs. Those footholds come only from auth_dc and auth_adfs, both requiring NOT mfa_admin. So mfa:admin cuts every path to exfiltrated. With no defences, a path exists: phish_workstation, pivot_internal, auth_appserver, kerberoast_dc, auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db, exfiltrate_db. So the minimum is 1."
